2026-11-28T02:05:00.4672820Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4674180Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4674720Z 
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4675310Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4685650Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4685980Z 
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4686240Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4687370Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4687980Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4688590Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4689020Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4689330Z 
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4689740Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4690160Z 
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4690440Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4691070Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4691610Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4691880Z 
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4692070Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4692550Z   printf '%s\n' export\ PATH\=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:\$PATH >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4692930Z 
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4693130Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4694210Z   export LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4694650Z   export CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4694890Z 
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4695070Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-28T02:05:00.4695510Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm
